Oscillator candidate:
SiTime SiT8008BC-22-33E-12.288000G

Specifications:
- Frequency: 12.288 MHz
- Supply: 3.3 V
- Output: LVCMOS, with output enable
- Frequency stability: +/-25 ppm
- Package: 3.2 x 2.5 mm, four pads
- Operating temperature: -20 to +70 degrees C
- One oscillator per transmitter/receiver board

Proposed clock architecture:
- Oscillator output connects to TAC5112 GPI1, pin 12.
- Net name: CODEC_CCLK.
- Firmware configures GPI1 as the codec reference-clock input.
- TAC5112 generates I2S BCLK and FSYNC.
- nRF54L15 operates as an I2S slave.
- Receiver audio data flows from nRF54L15 to codec DIN.

Target audio timing:
- Sample rate / FSYNC: 44.1 kHz
- Two 16-bit I2S slots per frame
- BCLK: 1.4112 MHz (44,100 x 2 x 16)
- Mono guitar signal duplicated into both playback channels
- Wireless payload remains mono: 705.6 kbit/s before overhead

Synchronization:
- Transmitter and receiver use independent local audio clocks.
- Receiver firmware must compensate for clock drift.
- Proposed method: adaptive software resampling controlled by
  receiver buffer occupancy.

Separate radio clock:
- Each nRF54L15 requires its own 32 MHz reference crystal.
- The audio oscillator does not replace the radio crystal.

